# What the build context is allowed to contain.
#
# Deny-by-default, for the same reason .gitignore is: enumerating what to
# exclude fails the moment a new directory appears, and here the failure is not
# merely embarrassing but slow enough to look like a hang. `data/` on this
# checkout is 75 GB (69 GB of it captured documents, 2.5 GB of database
# backups). Docker tars the whole context and ships it to the daemon before it
# reads the first line of the Dockerfile, so a single missing exclusion turns a
# 90-second build into a 75 GB copy — and, worse, bakes subscriber endpoints
# and the VAPID private key into an image layer that anyone who pulls the image
# can read back.
#
# So: exclude everything, then re-admit exactly the paths the image needs.
*

# The package and its build metadata.
!pyproject.toml
!src/

# config.toml is committed and holds no secrets — paths, tuning and rate limits
# only (the VAPID key is a *path* into data/secrets, never the key itself), so
# it belongs in the image as the default configuration. TENDERS_CONFIG or a
# bind mount overrides it at run time.
!config.toml

# The long-running loops and the two self-healing jobs. scripts/ is not part of
# the installed package — the systemd units invoke these by path — so they have
# to be copied in explicitly rather than arriving with `pip install`.
!scripts/

# The unit files themselves are not used inside the container, but the
# entrypoint and the supervisor config live alongside them and every process
# definition in supervisord.conf cites the unit it replicates. Keeping them in
# the image means the reasoning is readable from inside a running container.
!deploy/

!README.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Re-excluded after the re-admissions above, because `!src/` would otherwise
# drag these in.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Build artefacts of a *host* install. An egg-info directory copied into the
# image describes a package installed at /home/…/projects/tender, and pip will
# happily believe it.
**/*.egg-info/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc

# ARCHITECTURE.md is deliberately absent from this list. It is the internal
# deployment runbook — it names the production host, its address, its home
# directory paths and a second person who has nothing to do with this image —
# and .gitignore excludes it from the public repository for exactly that
# reason. A file that is too sensitive to publish in a git repo is too
# sensitive to publish in a container image, and images get pushed to
# registries far more casually than commits get pushed to remotes.
